  "result": "I implemented `satisfies(version, range)` in `src/semver.js` following `docs/SPEC.md`, and `npm test` passes (4 tests, 0 failures).\n\nI added `test/semver.test.js`. It covers:\n- exact matches\n- X-ranges\n- operators on partial versions\n- tilde, caret and hyphen ranges\n- `||` sets\n- the prerelease rules\n- invalid versions and ranges\n- non-string input\n\nSome choices where the spec was silent:\n- **Prerelease identifiers:** a numeric one with a leading zero (such as `1.0.0-01`) is accepted, because the spec only bans leading zeros in major, minor and patch.\n- **Invalid ranges:** a wildcard followed by a number (`1.x.3`) is invalid, and so is a prerelease on a partial version (`1.2-beta`).\n- **`>*` and `<*`:** both match nothing.\n- **Hyphen ranges:** a hyphen range can be combined with other comparators in the same set, and they are ANDed.",
